":["A long-lived MCP server processing thousands of gate ops accumulates unbounded `.rebar/gate_runs/<job_id>` files"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a max-age / on-completion prune for `.rebar/gate_runs/` mirroring the registry's max-age sweep, and document it alongside the workflow_runs cleanup.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify follower behavior when the shared singleflight computation fails: propagate the exception to all awaiting callers (and purge the key) so followers can re-invoke, and add a test asserting a raising fake propagates to both concurrent callers.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5b","E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'a second concurrent caller for the same key awaits the SAME computation and shares its verdict'","'Purge-on-completion + a defensive max-age sweep' — describes success/timeout cleanup but not exception propagation","review_plan/verify_completion wrap an external LLM four-pass which can fail; the plan's tests only cover the success verdict ('both get the same verdict') not the shared-failure case"],"finding":"Phase 1's in-process singleflight registry does not specify how a FAILED shared computation (the wrapped LLM gate raising an exception) is propagated to concurrent followers awaiting the same key.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4079c88a4d66bbef","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approved remediation — Phase 1 (src/rebar/_mcp_inflight.py); Fix plan — tests","norm_id":"na97038fee73d10ed","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Leader run raises mid-LLM-pass (network/API error); followers are left either hanging until the max-age sweep or silently returning a stale/absent verdict"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that a leader exception is captured and re-raised to every follower awaiting the key, the key is purged on failure (not left for max-age sweep), and add a test: fake raises ⇒ both concurrent same-key callers observe the failure and the key is immediately re-invokable.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the atomic register-or-attach primitive (e.g. a lock/CAS around key insertion) in `_mcp_inflight.py` so two same-key callers cannot both start a run under a check-then-act race.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'an in-process singleflight registry (a second concurrent caller for the same key awaits the SAME computation and shares its verdict)' — states the outcome, not the atomic register-or-attach primitive","T9 CONCURRENCY SAFETY: 'Shared/mutable state mutated atomically (lock/CAS/transaction, no check-then-act TOCTOU)'"],"finding":"The dedup registry's core correctness depends on two near-simultaneous same-key callers atomically resolving to a single computation, but the plan states the behavior ('a second concurrent caller ... awaits the SAME computation') without naming the concurrency primitive (lock / atomic get-or-create) that closes the check-then-act TOCTOU window — the exact race the -32001 retry storm produces.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f12457a9c7e060252","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approved remediation — Phase 1 / `_mcp_inflight.py` in-process singleflight registry","norm_id":"n1b53ad77c21bad62","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two -32001-driven retries arrive within the same scheduler tick; both miss the key and both start a billable LLM run, defeating AC #2"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Document that registration uses a lock (or atomic setdefault of a future/event) so the second caller deterministically attaches to the leader's computation.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"